@slim: 1.0
@+project: day-01-openapi-test-generator
@+stack: java-11, maven, gemini

# Structure
Practice/
  content-plan.md — LinkedIn post schedule
  poc/day-01-openapi-test-generator/ — Day 1 POC

# What It Does
Multi-agent system reading Swagger/OpenAPI spec (URL or file), calling Gemini, generating
BDD (Cucumber + REST Assured) or TDD (TestNG + REST Assured) — controlled by config.properties.

# Commands
=== BUILD [bash]
cd poc/day-01-openapi-test-generator
mvn compile
mvn compile exec:java
mvn package
java -jar target/openapi-test-generator-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar
=== /BUILD

# Setup
1. Get Gemini API key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
2. Open src/main/resources/config.properties
3. Set gemini.api.key, swagger.url, test.style

# Architecture
config.properties → Main → AgentConfig → ConfigValidator
                         → OrchestratorAgent
                               → SpecFetcherAgent    (SwaggerFetcherSkill: URL or file)
                               → SpecAnalyzerAgent   (SnakeYAML/Jackson, no LLM)
                               → BDDGeneratorAgent   (4 Gemini calls)
                                 OR TDDGeneratorAgent (3 Gemini calls)
                               → FileWriterAgent     (FileWriterSkill)

# Package Layout
- agents/ — orchestration and workflow
- skills/ — reusable infrastructure (HTTP, file I/O, LLM transport)
- instructions/ — prompt builders (static methods, no LLM calls)
- rules/ — config validation and generation policy
- config/ — AgentConfig from config.properties
- model/ — SpecSummary, GeneratedFile value objects

~ Step defs generated AFTER feature file with its content as context — ensures annotation match
~ Java 11 LTS only — no records, text blocks, or switch expressions
